Subject: Diagnostic: the sync test uses the deterministic AI clocks
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Rollback study. Offline, cGame::BeginGame gives the AI a script time budget
of one real millisecond and the real ticker as its profiling clock: a script
whose measured time nears the budget is skipped at random. Network and
recorded games, which must be deterministic, turn the budget off and use the
simulation clock. Under RECHARGED_SYNCTEST offline matches take that
deterministic branch too, as a rollback session will. Nothing else that
depends on IsNetworkOrRecordedGame changes. Without RECHARGED_SYNCTEST the
game is unchanged.

diff --git a/src/Game/Game.cpp b/src/Game/Game.cpp
index 1a6cf4e..761ff5b 100644
--- a/src/Game/Game.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/Game.cpp
@@ -1,4 +1,7 @@
 #include "Game/NetworkMessageRegistry.h"
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+#include "mscharged_synctest.h"
+#endif
 #include "Game/DetInput.h"
 #include "Game/AI/TeamPlayMachine.h"
 #ifdef MSCHARGED_NATIVE
@@ -885,6 +888,16 @@ void cGame::BeginGame(bool bRematch, bool bStraightToKickoff)
         gAIProfilingClock = GetGameTickerMilliseconds;
         gAIActivityClock = GetGameSimulationMilliseconds;
     }
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+    // The sync test runs offline matches with the deterministic AI clocks of
+    // network and recorded games: no real-time script budget.
+    if (mscharged_synctest_active())
+    {
+        SetScriptTimeBudget(-1.0f);
+        gAIProfilingClock = GetGameSimulationMilliseconds;
+        gAIActivityClock = GetGameSimulationMilliseconds;
+    }
+#endif
 }
 void cGame::CheckForGoal()
 {
